ditions more than the exchange rate (typical for domestically focused companies).","BIMAS (5 years): +1.250,3 % in lira, +169,3 % in dollars (+21,9 % a year). USD/TRY moved +401,3 % over the same period.","BIMAS FX beta 0,35 (60 months, correlation 0,12): partial pass-through; part of each lira move becomes a loss in dollars.","Damodaran’s country risk premium for Turkey is 4,66% (Moody’s Ba3): the extra return equity investors ask over a mature market. Total equity risk premium 8,89%."],"notes":["Dollar price = lira price / USDTRY (same day; the last rate is carried over Turkish holidays). Prices are adjusted for bonus issues and dividends.","FX beta = slope of the monthly lira return on the monthly USD/TRY change. Near 1 the stock fully prices lira weakness (flat in dollars); near 0 the lira price ignores the rate. With a low correlation the beta is noisy; read it as rough.","No inflation adjustment: a high lira return during high inflation need not be a real gain; the dollar view is a rough check.","Add your free TCMB EVDS key to also get CPI-adjusted (real) returns and a check against the official exchange rate."],"sources":[{"label":"Yahoo Finance prices (adjusted for splits and dividends)","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/"},{"label":"Yahoo Finance USD/TRY (USDTRY=X)","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/USDTRY=X/"},{"label":"KAP — Public Disclosure Platform (annual reports, for the FX revenue share)","url":"https://www.kap.org.tr/"},{"label":"Damodaran Online (NYU Stern): implied ERP, country risk premiums, industry averages (US)","url":"https://pages.stern.nyu.edu/~adamodar/New_Home_Page/datacurrent.html"}],"warnings":[],"inputs":{"fx_symbol":"USDTRY=X","index":"XU100.IS","fx_revenue_pct":null},"asof":"2026-11-15","disclaimer":"Educational analysis of historical price data; not investment advice.","highlights":[],"quality":{"passed":1,"checked":1,"warnings":0,"failed":0,"items":[{"id":"prices","label":"Price data is current","status":"pass","detail":"USDTR